{"id": "sevt_01HXJvKonGyGvow9gPe5iVgN", "content": [{"text": "Checkout deploy `a3f9c21` caused the 500s. It replaced one batched query with a query per order row, which exhausted the DB connection pool.\n\n**Timeline**\n- **14:31:** Checkout deploy `a3f9c21` (\"refactor order summary builder for readability\"). p99 latency goes from about 75 ms to about 3.8 s in the same minute.\n- **14:40:** Error rate climbs from 0 to 25\u201365%, about 9 minutes after the deploy.\n- **Other deploys:** cart (09:14), auth (11:02) and inventory (14:55) don't line up. Inventory came after the latency jump.\n\n**Diff**\n`CheckoutSummaryHandler.build_summary` used to run one `order_items WHERE order_id IN (...)` query and group the results in memory. It now runs `OrderItem.objects.filter(order_id=...)` inside a loop over orders, which is an N+1 query pattern.\n\n**Log**\n- Before the deploy, checkout logged only the batched `IN (?)` query (134 occurrences).\n- After the deploy, it logged 3,320 per-row `order_id = ?` queries and only 3 batched ones.\n- Checkout logged 70 `DB connection pool exhausted (active=50/50, waiters=12)` errors.\n- The 500s are `PoolTimeout` errors on `/api/checkout/validate` (26), `/summary` (25) and `/submit` (19).\n- The auth `idp.internal` timeouts at 14:15 started before the deploy and are a separate issue. They don't explain the checkout errors.\n\n**Fix:** Revert `a3f9c21`, or restore the batched query and keep the explicit loop for readability.\n\n> **Root cause:** `a3f9c21` \u2014 the refactor turned the batched order-items query into one query per order row, which exhausted checkout's 50-connection DB pool and caused `PoolTimeout` 500s.", "type": "text"}], "processed_at": "2026-10-14T04:50:49.301939Z", "type": "agent.message"}
